"Visual overhaul and UX fixes for the Waldorf community task manager (Hungarian UI). (1) Hungarian line breaking: role names like \"Csoportadminisztrátor\" / \"Szuperadminisztrátor\" wrap mid-word without syllable hyphenation (e.g. \"Csoportadminisztrát/or\"); fix with proper Hungarian hyphenation/word-break rules (lang=\"hu\", hyphens, sizing) so names break correctly or fit. (2) On the test-profile chooser, each role card should itself be the clickable button; remove the separate \"Profil használata\" button. (3) In the parent task list, each task card (e.g. \"Kerti előkészítés – Firefox próba\") should be fully clickable; remove the separate \"Részletek\" link. (4) On the group admin overview, the summary cards (Nyitott jóváhagyások, Nyilvántartások, Feladatok és események, Függőben lévő kérelmek) should be clickable and navigate to the matching list (e.g. clicking \"Nyitott jóváhagyások\" shows the 3 open approvals). Apply UI/UX best practices and UI skills throughout (accessibility, focus states, touch targets, hover/active feedback, responsive layout). Branding: use the kindergarten logo at public/brand/logo.png (transparent) and cover photo public/brand/cover.jpg as the cover/background, and derive a Waldorf-friendly colour scheme from the photo of the kindergarten building (warm terracotta/red-brown roof and wood, orange-yellow walls, garden greens, blue flowers) plus the logo purple. Branch feature/visual-overhaul already exists locally."
